The library has LogIt's exercises, cardio activities and mobility drills, with cues for each. Add your
own with + and they show up in every picker. Your coach can share theirs with you; LogIt's and your
coach's items have Make my own copy if you want to change them.

## The tour on the phone

<HowTo id="app.exercises" />

## Your places and their machines

On the phone, Settings › Your places holds where you train: a gym, home, a work gym. Each place lists what's there: the bar and plates, dumbbells (fixed pairs or an adjustable set), kettlebells, other kit like a rack or a pull-up bar, and its machines. Machines are only kept in places. You don't have to set one up first: add a machine from a workout (tap the machine under the exercise's name) and your first one makes a place called My gym. An exercise's How to tab shows which machine you use at each place.

A machine is anything that decides the number you log: a weight stack, a plate-loaded machine like a leg press, or a Smith machine. Benches, racks and combo stations aren't machines, because bench press is the bar and its plates on any bench; tick them under Also here instead, along with an EZ or trap bar and what it weighs. A machine belongs to its place and serves every exercise you do on it, so a cable station is set up once. To add one, say how the weight goes on (a pin in a stack, plates you load, an assisted machine, or no weight), then read the numbers off the stack. Many stacks go up 5 kg at a time for the first plates and 10 kg after that: add a run for each change, or type every number exactly as printed. Tell Logit if you can add a little more (clip-on add-ons, or a pin with plates), so the weights it plans are ones you can actually set.

You can mark a machine out of order, coming soon or removed, and pick the days you usually train at each place. Machines you'd set up on exercises before this move into your first place (or My gym) by themselves.
